    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Company power phrase</h2>
    <p>The 12 June 2026 prospectus says the two sites together provide about 1 gigawatt of compute power, with more capacity available.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Southaven</h2>
    <p>Southaven sits at 2875 Stanton Road. As of 30 July 2026, 69 temporary gas turbines were powering the site. The company said a 1.2 gigawatt plant of 41 permanent turbines is under construction. A state permit from 11 March 2026 is for those 41. The company said temporary turbines start coming off as early as August 2026 and are gone by July 2027.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Memphis grid</h2>
    <p>Undated company page: a finished substation rated 150 megawatts, which the company says cost $35 million, plus a second substation at $20 million.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Vera and Rubin</h2>
    <p>On 24 August 2026 Nvidia said it will put Vera processors and Vera Rubin chips into this build, including a planned Starmind satellite.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Capabilities</h2>
    <p>From the live Colossus page, fetched 13 Sep 2026: 170 PB/s aggregate memory bandwidth; 2.8 Tb/s per-server network; 0.5 EB storage. Series C called out NVIDIA Spectrum-X Ethernet for the 100k to 200k path.</p>

